class SkillsViewQuery(BaseModel):
    where: str | None = Field('prj_projects.pk > 0', description="SQL WHERE clause selecting which branches of the hierarchy are returned. Any table of the hierarchy may be filtered on, not only prj_projects: cur_curricula, cur_type_degree, aoe_2_cur, aoe_area_of_operational_expertises, ops_2_aoe_2_cur, ops_operational_skills, ops_uses, ops_levels, pec_2_ops_2_aoe_2_cur, pec_performance_criteria, pec_learning_locations and pec_levels. Every column must be qualified with its table name - an unqualified name is ambiguous across the hierarchy and is rejected. Conditions combine with AND, OR and NOT, may be grouped with parentheses, and use the usual SQL operators. A condition on a deeper table prunes the whole tree to the branches satisfying it: filtering on a curriculum returns only the projects holding it, and only that curriculum inside them. Two limits apply. The translated *_txt fields are resolved from tsl_translations at read time and are not columns, so filter the stored tsl_* key instead. And statement keywords (SELECT, DELETE, CREATE, ...) are stripped from the clause before it is used, including inside quoted literals, so a string value containing one of them is silently altered. Examples:\n- `prj_projects.pk = 1` - one project with everything below it\n- `prj_projects.pk = 1 AND cur_curricula.pk = 32` - a single curriculum of that project\n- `prj_projects.pk = 1 AND (cur_curricula.pk = 30 OR cur_curricula.pk = 32)` - two of them\n- `cur_curricula.pk IN (30, 32)` - the same, with the project derived from the curricula\n- `aoe_area_of_operational_expertises.pk = 342` - every branch leading to that area\n- `cur_curricula.pk = 32 AND ops_operational_skills.tsl_title IS NOT NULL` - levels combined\n- `prj_projects.pk = 1 AND cur_curricula.created_at > '2020-01-01'` - non-key columns", title='Where')
    limit: int | None = Field(None, description='Maximum number of rows to return', title='Limit')
    offset: int | None = Field(None, description='Number of rows to skip', title='Offset')
    language: TslLanguageType | None = Field('de', description='Language used for translated fields', title='Language')


